@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Use — Kaarigar";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_AuthLayout.cshtml";
    var lastUpdated = "26 July 2026";
}

<!-- NAV -->
<partial name="_MarketingNav" />

<section class="k-legal">
    <div class="k-container k-legal__container">
        <a href="/" class="k-legal__back">&larr; Back to Home</a>

        <h1 class="k-legal__title">Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="k-legal__updated">Last updated: @lastUpdated</p>

        <div class="k-legal__notice">
            This is a general-purpose template covering how Kaarigar's platform works today.
            It is provided as a starting point and has not been reviewed by a lawyer —
            please have it checked against applicable Indian law (including the IT Act,
            DPDP Act 2023, and any state shops &amp; establishment / staffing regulations)
            before relying on it in production.
        </div>

        <p>
            These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern access to and use of the Kaarigar platform
            (the "Platform"), including the website and any related mobile experience,
            operated by Kaarigar ("Kaarigar", "we", "us", "our"). By registering for an
            account or otherwise using the Platform, you ("you", "User") agree to be bound
            by these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Platform.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who Can Use Kaarigar</h2>
        <p>
            Kaarigar connects two kinds of Users: <strong>Employers</strong> (businesses,
            households, or individuals seeking workers) and <strong>Workers</strong>
            ("Kaarigar Partners" — electricians, plumbers, drivers, cooks, and other
            skilled/semi-skilled workers seeking jobs). You must be at least 18 years old
            and legally capable of entering into a binding contract to register.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Registration &amp; Verification</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>You must provide accurate, current information during registration, including a valid mobile number, which is verified via OTP.</li>
            <li>Workers must upload a valid government ID proof (Aadhaar, PAN, Voter ID, or Driving Licence). Employers must upload valid business proof (GST or Gumastha registration) where applicable.</li>
            <li>All accounts require Admin approval before becoming active. Kaarigar may approve, reject, or request additional documents at its discretion.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and for all activity under your account.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. The Role Kaarigar Plays</h2>
        <p>
            Kaarigar is a platform that helps Employers and Workers find each other. Kaarigar
            is <strong>not</strong> the employer of any Worker, and does not itself hire,
            supervise, or direct work performed. Any job or engagement arranged through the
            Platform is a direct arrangement between the Employer and the Worker. Employers
            are responsible for ensuring the work offered complies with applicable labour
            laws, safety standards, and wage regulations.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Job Posting &amp; Applications</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Employers are responsible for the accuracy of job postings, including required skills, location, timing, and the hourly rate offered.</li>
            <li>Workers may browse and express interest in job postings. An Employer viewing or contacting an applicant does not, by itself, create a binding obligation on either party to proceed.</li>
            <li>Job start and completion are confirmed using one-time passwords (Job Starting OTP and Satisfaction OTP) generated by the Employer and entered by the Worker. Both parties are responsible for completing this verification honestly and accurately.</li>
            <li>Either party may cancel an application before the job starts, with a reason recorded for transparency.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Payments</h2>
        <p>
            Unless explicitly stated otherwise on the Platform, Kaarigar does not currently
            process, hold, or guarantee payment of wages between Employers and Workers.
            Payment terms are agreed directly between the Employer and Worker. If and when
            Kaarigar introduces in-platform payments, separate payment terms will apply and
            will be presented for your acceptance at that time.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Notifications</h2>
        <p>
            By registering, you consent to receive service-related communications from
            Kaarigar via SMS, WhatsApp, and/or email — including OTPs, job alerts, and
            status updates on applications. You may opt out of non-essential notifications
            (such as job-match alerts) from your profile settings; essential account and
            security messages cannot be opted out of.
        </p>

        <h2>7. User Conduct</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Provide false, misleading, or fraudulent information, including fake documents or job postings.</li>
            <li>Use the Platform for any unlawful purpose, or to harass, threaten, or discriminate against another User.</li>
            <li>Attempt to circumvent the Platform's verification, OTP, or approval processes.</li>
            <li>Interfere with the security or proper functioning of the Platform.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Content &amp; Documents You Provide</h2>
        <p>
            You retain ownership of documents and information you upload (ID proofs,
            business proofs, resumes, photos). You grant Kaarigar a limited licence to
            store and process this content solely to operate the Platform — including
            verification by Admin and, where relevant, sharing necessary details (such as
            name and contact number) with the other party once an application proceeds.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            Our handling of your personal data, including what we collect and how it is
            used, shared, and retained, is described in our Privacy Policy. By using the
            Platform you also agree to that Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Account Suspension &amp; Termination</h2>
        <p>
            Kaarigar may suspend or terminate an account at its discretion, including where
            a User provides false information, is found to violate these Terms, or is the
            subject of credible complaints from other Users. Users may also request deletion
            of their account by contacting Kaarigar.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Disclaimers &amp; Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
            The Platform is provided "as is." Kaarigar does not guarantee the availability,
            conduct, skill, reliability, or reputation of any Employer or Worker, and is not
            responsible for the outcome of any engagement arranged through the Platform,
            including disputes over pay, work quality, or workplace incidents. To the
            maximum extent permitted by law, Kaarigar's liability arising from use of the
            Platform is limited to the fullest extent permitted under applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
            We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected
            by updating the "Last updated" date above, and continued use of the Platform
            after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
            Questions about these Terms can be directed to Kaarigar support through the
            contact details provided on the Platform.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

